--- body ---
## Context

`erg ready` reports a ticket as "claimed" when any git branch *contains*
the ticket ID as a substring. Date-stamped branch names defeat this:
`quickpr/docs-add-econom-ia-2026-conference-progr-20260604-061904`
contains "0260" (inside `20260604`), so ticket 0260 (Write Exp2 H6
section) was reported claimed although nobody works on it. Every
quickpr/* branch created on 2026-06-04 shadows 0260 and 0604; on
2026-12-31 it would shadow 0261 and 1231, etc.

Consequence: falsely-claimed tickets disappear from the ready list, so
pick-ticket/raid sweeps silently skip real work for as long as any
same-day quickpr branch lives.

## Relevant files

- `tickets/tools/go/` — erg source (claim detection in the ready
  command); upstream is the git-erg project
- `scripts/quickpr.sh` — generates the date-stamped branch names that
  trigger the collision

## Actions

1. Tighten the claim heuristic to match the ID at a path/word boundary,
   e.g. branch matches `(^|/)t?<ID>([-_/]|$)` — `t0260`, `ticket/0260-…`,
   `0260-slug` claim; `…-20260604-…` does not.
2. Add a unit test in the erg test suite: branch
   `quickpr/x-20260604-061904` must NOT claim ticket 0260; branch
   `t0260` and `ticket/0260-fix` must.
3. Rebuild the committed `tickets/erg` binary; consider upstreaming to
   git-erg.

## Test

Red step: with a branch named `quickpr/x-20260604-1` present, `erg
ready --json` currently reports id 0260 with claimed=true; after the
fix it reports claimed=false.

## Exit criteria

- Date-stamped branches no longer claim numerically-colliding tickets
- Boundary-form branches (tNNNN, ticket/NNNN-…) still claim
- erg test covers both cases; committed binary rebuilt
